    intro: 'A holiday photoshoot in the Douro hands visitors something their own cameras never manage: a record of the trip with the travellers standing in it. Typical stays in the valley are short — a night or two at a quinta, a rail excursion up from Porto, a tasting weekend — and the person holding the phone is permanently missing from the pictures. Booking {duration} with a photographer who already knows which bank catches the light at which hour fixes that. One location, chosen for your timetable, and you go home with frames of your family or friends as well as of the terraces.',
