    intro: 'Personal branding photography in the Douro makes particular sense for people whose work is bound to the place: a winemaker launching a label under their own name, a guide who walks visitors through the terraces, a chef, a quinta owner who hosts guests and runs the social accounts alone. Their brand is half them and half the valley, and stock imagery misses both. This session builds a library in one sitting — {duration}, two or three settings, {photos} photographs — with vertical and horizontal versions so the same frames serve a website, a brochure and a year of posts.',
